# No AI Attribution

When creating commit messages, pull request descriptions, code comments, changelog entries, or any other authored artifact, **do not add yourself (Claude, Cursor, or any AI assistant) as a contributor, co-author, or author**.

## Rules

- **No `Co-Authored-By:` trailers** referencing Claude, Cursor, Anthropic, Codex, Copilot, GPT, or any AI assistant.
- **No `Generated-by:` / `Authored-by:` lines** referencing AI tools.
- **No "Generated with [tool]" footers**, badges, or links in commits, PR bodies, or release notes.
- **No emojis or signatures** like "Robot says…", "🤖 Generated by…", etc.
- **No "Made with Cursor / Claude / AI" comments** in source files.
- The author of every commit must be the human user from their existing git config — never modify `user.name` or `user.email`.

## Examples

```
# BAD — never write commits like this
Refactor resume button into single CTA

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Generated with Cursor.
```

```
# GOOD — clean, human-attributed
Refactor resume button into single CTA
```

## Scope

Applies to: commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, issue comments, release notes, README/CHANGELOG entries, and any code comments authored during the session.
